 chris bill are your multiplex  kits limited to seven targets  you mentioned using nine opals how is  the spectra on mixing  so that's a good question so in my  presentation i talked about  doing six mark biomarkers plus dappy  recently about a little over a year ago  we came out with two new opal dies so  that allows us to do eight biomarkers  plus dappy  on the vector polaris  we have two there's two options you can  do whole slide seven color staining  um and then you can also do field of  view nine color staining  thank you our next question  um so let's come back to you your  presentation talks about  a seven color stain but i only want to  do  three or four markers is that possible  absolutely um so yeah generally um what  i what i showed  here today was that seven color um we do  sell kits that  um stain for four colors so that's  absolutely doable  and it's in to be honest it's a good way  to start  staining for opal start start low and  then increase as you go on  thank you now what was used on the  cytokeratin c11 clone as far as  mlm  as bill mentioned that clone is  biotinylated  so there was no reason to we didn't have  to detect it with  anti-mouse hrp so that's how we avoided  any mouse on mouse cross reactivity in  that setting  using just an unconjugated mouse  monoclonal primary antibody  you would run into issues with uh  secondary detection and mouse on mouse  reactivity  got it thank you  how would i get the protocols for using  multiple opal dyes on  same species antibodies  we have on opals akoya i mean on  koibaio.com  under resources we have a protocols page  where we have a couple of different  protocols for  seven color stains one one being a mouse  protocol  and then i can also share  my protocol as well  okay good thank you bill okay  our next question and again bear with me  we've got so many great questions coming  in and i want to make sure that  i answer once that everyone is asking um  how about this one is cst  developing validated