ng opal ab  colors if you are getting a lot of  background  um so that's a good question so there's  a couple of levers you can change when  optimizing an opal stain the first is  your primary antibody if you're getting  background then  it's probably your primary antibody that  needs to be diluted out further  if you're seeing your signal intensities  too high then you it would dilute your  opal dies  thank you our next question  uh does cst have a good anti-mouse pan  ck  antibody preferably not raised in mouth  um the the only option we have right now  for a pan cytokeratin antibody  is the one that bill spoke about in the  panel  during this presentation um as we  mentioned  the particular variant he used  is conjugated to biotin  which helps us reduce or helps us avoid  any muscle  mouse cross reactivity um we don't  currently have  a rabbit monoclonal uh that detects  pan cytokeratin in ffpe tissues  at this time  okay our next question i have an  antibody that does not work  well with dab but has been shown to work  with directly conjugated secondary fl  antibodies will it work with opal  yeah so um in this instance you know i  guess when i see that  it's working with the secondary  fluorescent antibody  i'm surprised that it's not working with  dab but that being said  um since it's working with your  secondary conjugate  since opal is actually amplifying it  even more than your secondary conjugate  um then then you should be able to get  amplification of that antibody  and so it should work with opal  very good thank you let's see  uh let's go with our next question  let's go here  yes let's take this question can i use  an antibody created in a species  other than mouth or rabbit for example  rat  uh yes you can uh basically with the  opal  technology and the opal kits you can use  an anybody  that was raised in any species  the limiting factor would be having an  hrp conjugated secondary antibody  that detects uh in anybody raised in  your  in your specie